Oh, that comment was on a different page. I agree, {sa} probably shouldn't =
be in those see-also lists at all as it's not really related to BAhE. Consi=
der my proposals amended to remove LEhU from the definition of {bu} and rem=
ove {sa} from the see-also lists of {ba'e} and {za'e}.

On Thursday, June 12, 2014 at 12:02 PM, Alex Burka wrote:

> SI, SA, and SU are all separate selma'o so presumably SU should be in tha=
t list as well. I'll remove LEhU.
> =20
> On Thursday, June 12, 2014 at 7:35 AM, Jorge Llamb=C3=ADas wrote:
> =20
> > =20
> > =20
> > =20
> > On Thu, Jun 12, 2014 at 12:54 AM, Alex Burka <aburka@seas.upenn.edu (ma=
ilto:aburka@seas.upenn.edu)> wrote:
> > > bu
> > > Combines with the previous word to make a Lojban letteral, provided t=
hat it is not one of the quote cmavo (ZO, ZOI, LOhU, LEhU) or one of the er=
asure cmavo (SI, SA, SU), ZEI, or FAhO. If the aforementioned previous word=
 is already a letteral, the resulting letteral will not necessarily be the =
same, for instance, "ky. bu" is different from "ky". In addition to single =
words, bu can be combined with a letteral that is already a composite of a =
word+bu, a zei-lujvo, a zo-quoted word, a lo'u-quoted string of words or a =
zoi-quoted foreign text. If there is no previous word, "bu" is in error; th=
is entails that "bu bu" by itself is also ungrammatical.
> > =20
> > LEhU shouldn't be there, it's at most a magic word assistant, not a mag=
ic word. "le'u bu", "le'u zei valsi", "le'u si" should be fine, unless le'u=
 has already been claimed by lo'u, but that's no different than for any oth=
er word. LEhU is like a zoi-delimiter, except LOhU always brings its own as=
sistant whereas ZOI picks one from the members of the public. =20
> >  =20
> > > ba'e (BAhE)
> > > Emphasize next word. Forethought emphasis indicator. Indicates that n=
ext word is especially emphasized or emphatic. For grammatical purposes, "b=
a'e" marks the following word but does not change its nature. (The construc=
t behaves just as the marked word by itself.) The two words are considered =
distinct for "sa" matching purposes. Multiple BAhE cmavo may be used in suc=
cession, and they combine to mark the next non-BAhE word. =20
> > > See also za'e, .ui, sa, "Magic Words".
> > > =20
> > > Keywords: Emphasize next word, emphasize next.
> > > =20
> > > =20
> > > =20
> > =20
> > =20
> > Not sure why "sa" is mentioned specifically.
> >  =20
> > mu'o mi'e xorxes
